    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="0853" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860c.01/51</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5805</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 9, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received November 27</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith, in
                    copy and translation, a report on the situation in Poland which has been brought
                    to me by Mr. Marjan Seyda, member of the Polish National Committee which formed
                    the subject of the Department’s telegram No. 2703 of October 8 last.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d717-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am informed that the periodical reports of Mr. Seyda were formerly given to the
                    American Minister at Berne.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. G. Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d717-a1.xml" xpointer="d717-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
